WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.030
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.699
Alice and Bob can complete a job in two hours.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.529
Alice and Charlie can complete the same job in three hours.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.760
Bob and Charlie can complete the same job in four hours.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.120
How long will the job take if Alice, Bob, and Charlie work together?

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.800
Assume each person works at a constant rate whether working alone or working with others.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.700
This problem has been asked to students in US colleges.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.760
To the professor's surprise,

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:41.550
many of the students set up the wrong equations and could not solve this problem.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.730
Can you figure it out?

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.559
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:00:54.129 --> 00:01:00.179
Before I get to the solution, let me go over a common mistake in how students get to the wrong answer.

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:06.298
They read the first sentence, that Alice and Bob can complete a job in two hours,

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.419
and translate the names and the numbers into an equation.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:14.069
They say this must mean that A + B = 2.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:20.129
They look at the second sentence, that Alice and Charlie can complete the job in three hours,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.180
and they similarly convert it to A + C = 3.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.040
The third condition, that Bob and Charlie can complete the job in four hours,

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.360
gets converted to the equation B + C = 4.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.180
The question of how long it will take for all three of them working together

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:45.940
gets translated into the question
of "what is A + B + C  = ?"

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.720
So to solve this system of equations...

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.420
They want to solve for A + B + C, so they can add up all the equations together.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.680
We end up getting two terms of A, two terms of B, and two terms of C,

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.520
to equal 2 + 3 + 4.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:11.340
If we group the factors [summands], we get
2A + 2B + 2C = 9.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:17.049
We then divide by two and that gets us to

00:02:17.049 --> 00:02:20.319
A + B + C = 9/2 = 4.5 (four and a half).

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:24.519
So evidently this will be the answer that many students get.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.940
They would say that it takes 4.5 hours for all three of them, when working together.

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:35.499
But let's think about: does this answer make any sense?

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:38.829
We know that Alice and Bob take two hours,

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:44.199
Alice and Charlie take three hours and Bob and Charlie take four hours,

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.760
but somehow when all three are working together they take four and a half hours?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.740
This makes no sense. When three people work together it should take less time then when only two people work together!

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:02.500
But 4.5 hours is more time, so this answer must be wrong.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.500
Not only were the equations set up incorrectly,

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.600
but any student who submits this answer

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.200
is not thinking about whether the answer makes any logical sense.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.200
So how do we solve this problem?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:22.810
We need to set up the equations in the correct method. We know that Alice and Bob can complete a job in two hours,

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.039
so how do we translate this into an equation?

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:34.569
Well, if they complete the job in two hours, that means the percentage of the job that Alice does in two hours

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:41.620
plus the percentage of the job that Bob does in two hours equals 100%, or that equals 1.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.260
Now since they work at a constant rate,

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:50.200
we can say the amount of the job that Alice does in two hours is

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.229
2 times the amount of the job that she does in one hour.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.230
And the same thing goes for Bob.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.899
So we now have a natural choice for our variables

00:03:59.299 --> 00:04:06.879
we can say the percentage of the job that Alice does in one hour will be the variable A, and the

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:10.899
percentage of the job that Bob does in one hour will be the variable B.

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:17.738
This leads to the equation that 2A + 2B = 1.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:28.400
And that's how we can translate this we can group this out to be 2 times (2x) the quantity A + B = 1.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:36.360
So we can now translate the second sentence. We have Alice and Charlie completing the job in three hours.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.800
This will translate into 3 times the quantity A + C = 1,

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.020
where C is the percentage of the job that Charlie completes in one hour.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.460
We also have that Bob and Charlie can complete the job in four hours,

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.620
so that would mean 4 times the quantity B + C = 1.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.400
Now we want to figure out... What would happen if they all three work together?

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.480
So we are needing to solve for...

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:12.220
the time (t) x (A + B + C) = 1.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.600
We need to solve for this variable "t".

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.340
So how do we do that?

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.979
Well, we can similarly add up all the equations

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:25.529
But we have different quantities of each of these variables, so in order to get the same number of each variable,

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.690
we're going to do a little trick.

00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:32.129
We're going to multiply each equation so that there's a leading coefficient of 12,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:35.249
which is the lowest common multiple of 2, 3 and 4, so

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.789
the first equation will multiply by six.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.169
This will get 12 times the quantity A + B to be equal to 6.

00:05:43.479 --> 00:05:49.199
The second equation will multiply by four and the third equation will multiply by three.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.680
We can now add up all of these equations

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.920
We'll end up with 12A (2 times),

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:04.280
12B (2 times), and 12C (2 times), and this will be equal to 6 + 4 + 3.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:11.580
We can factor out the 24 of each of these variables,

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:16.659
and that will be equal to 6 + 4 + 3, which equals 13.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.920
We now divide by 13...

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:26.740
and we end up with 24 divided by 13 times the quantity A + B + C = 1, and

00:06:27.729 --> 00:06:29.908
THAT is what we wanted to figure out.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:38.819
So we go back to our setup and we can see that we get to the answer of 24 over 13.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:45.090
So the job will take 24 over 13 hours or about 1 hour and 51 minutes.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:51.509
And this is a sensible answer because it takes less time than any pair working together.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.980
Did you figure this out?

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.610
Thanks for watching this video; please subscribe to my channel.

